    "reasoning": "Every field has a mathematically correct choice supported by its own captured worked solution. q-106: adding corresponding matrix entries gives rows (-12,-12,1) and (1,1,1). q-72382: u=1+x^5 transforms the integral into ∫u^(-1/2)du=2√u+C. q-2195: u=x^2+1 gives ∫u^12du=u^13/13+C. q-72467: u=x^2-5 gives (1/2)∫u^(1/2)du=u^(3/2)/3+C, equivalent to the displayed radical on the real domain u≥0. q-12496: u=x^4+11 gives (1/4)∫u^9du=u^10/40+C. q-49451: u=x^2+1 gives 2∫du/u=2ln(x^2+1)+C because x^2+1>0. q-72605: u=2-5x^5 gives -(2/5)∫du/u. q-113726: u=3-x^5 gives -(7/5)∫u^(-6)du=7/(25u^5)+C. q-12502: u=x^2+5 gives (1/2)∫u^(-10)du=-1/(18u^9)+C. Extra grouping braces in the integral choices do not change their values. q-46831: rationalization leaves 1/((x+2)(√(x+2)+2)), whose limit is 1/16. q-46830: rationalization leaves (√(3x-3)+3)/3, whose right-hand limit is 2. q-66896: taking logarithms gives x-1=x ln 3, hence x=1/(1-ln 3). q-10484: setting x=0 gives y^2=9 and intercepts (0,±3). q-84045: setting x=0 gives (y-5)^2=0 and intercept (0,5). q-8220 and q-16414: complex conjugation preserves the real part and reverses the imaginary part. No earlier submitted answer or revealed grade is supplied; confirmation rests on the captured worked solutions and independent mathematics.",
